  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat recorded $8.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 255 awards with an average award size of $33.7M, and obligations were down 59.8% year over year. Historical obligations show a multi-year pattern: FY21 $8.7B, FY22 $9.4B, FY23 $10.8B, FY24 $8.6B, and FY25 $21.4B. Engineering Services dominates Electric Boat’s portfolio at $6.9B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $1.7B. A cluster of small manufacturing markets together account for modest dollars, including Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.6M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. The mix and year-to-year swings indicate work concentrated in a few large programs plus a long tail of specialty manufacturing and R&D services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is Electric Boat's federal work by market?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for Electric Boat at $6.9B. Ship Building and Repairing is the second market at $1.7B. Remaining NAICS markets are small by comparison, with individual values ranging from $2.4M down to $267K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How volatile have Electric Boat's obligations been year to year?",
        "body": "Obligations rose and fell over the last six fiscal years, peaking at $21.4B in FY25 and returning to $8.6B in FY26 to date. FY21 was $8.7B, FY22 was $9.4B, FY23 was $10.8B, and FY24 was $8.6B, showing large variation driven by a few big awards."
      }
    ]
  },
